y.stanford.edu/sfx?url%5Fver=Z39.88-2004&ctx%5Fver=Z39.88-2004&ctx%5Fenc=info:ofi/enc:UTF-8&rfr%5Fid=info:sid/sfxit.com:opac%5F856&url%5Fctx%5Ffmt=info:ofi/fmt:kev:mtx:ctx&sfx.ignore%5Fdate%5Fthreshold=1&rft.object%5Fid=5300000000021376&svc%5Fval%5Ffmt=info:ofi/fmt:kev:mtx:sch%5Fsvc&xeLoaderURLxmr4xmr5300000000021376ffs2c68d8cd-de5d-50e4-83f9-603a463a3d8fi003a66f4-7ff4-5ff8-a20c-4d1882a15bf404856cam a2200709 i in0000016915920250403134755.0240810s2024    gw a     b    100 0 eng d7 a13328710462DE-101  a9783447122245qhardbound  a3447122242  z9783447395410qe-book3 a9783447122245 9ahar240210882  a(OCoLC)on1451853586  a(OCoLC-M)1451853586  aOHXbengerdacOHXdISBdOCLCOdISBdHULdOCLCOdUtOrBLW  afw-----af-et---ap------ai------ 4aBR290b.E27 202400aEarly South-South links in the history of world Christianity (16th - early 19th Century) /cedited by Klaus Koschorke, Ciprian Burlǎcioiu and Philipp Kuster 1aWiesbaden :bHarrassowitz Verlag,c2024  a271 pages :billustrations (chiefly color) ;c25 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aStudien zur aussereuropäischen Christentumsgeschichte (Asien, Afrika, Lateinamerika),x1611-0080 ;vBand 38 =aStudies in the history of Christianity in the Non-Western World (Asia, Africa, Latin America) ;vvolume 38  aPapers presented at an international and interdisciplinary conference held in Bad Homburg near Frankfurt (Germany),5-7 January 2023  a"It was by no means only Western missionaries who brought Christianity to the countries of the Global South. In various places they encountered old Christian churches which had been already existing such as in India and Ethiopia. In other places, voluntary or forced migration and indigenous Christian initiatives also led to an independent expansion and the formation of transregional networks at an early stage. This resulted in various exchange relationships between different areas of the expanding Christian world, which were carried out by local representatives. The volume contains the contributions of an international conference held in 2023, which discussed early examples of such South-South connections between the 16th and early 19th century. It not only provides important insights for a polycentric approach to the history of World Christianity, it also offers new perspectives on diverse discourses regarding the history of globalization and transcontinental religious entanglements." --cProvided by publisher  aIncludes bibliographical references 0aChurch historyyModern period, 1500-vCongresses. 0aAfrica, WestxChurch historyvCongresses. 0aEthiopiaxChurch historyvCongresses. 0aPacific AreaxChurch historyvCongresses. 0aIndian Ocean RegionxChurch historyvCongresses. 0aAfrica, WestxChurch history. 0aPacific AreaxChurch history. 0aChurch historyy16th century.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh95000560 0aChurch historyy17th century.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85025630 0aChurch historyy18th century.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85025631 0aChurch historyy19th century.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85025632 6aAfrique occidentalexHistoire religieuse. 6aPacifique, Région duxHistoire religieuse. 6aÉglisexHistoirey16e siècle. 6aÉglisexHistoirey17e siècle. 6aÉglisexHistoirey18e siècle. 6aÉglisexHistoirey19e siècle. 6aÉglisexHistoirey1500-vCongrès. 6aAfrique occidentalexHistoire religieusevCongrès. 6aPacifique, Région duxHistoire religieusevCongrès. 6aIndien, Région de l'océanxHistoire religieusevCongrès.1 aKoschorke, Klaus,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nr920254151https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJxcVYgTVv9TKgkcmjYVmd1 aBurlacioiu, Ciprian,d1976-eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20160335331https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJvcYHdFyP4VCP8FWBj6Kd1 aKuster, Philipp,eeditor.08