 aerospace engineering /cMykola Nechyporuk, Volodymyr Pavlikov, Dmytro Krytskyi, editors 1aCham :bSpringer,c[2024] 4c©2024  a1 online resource (vii, 283 pages) :billustrations (chiefly color)  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aStudies in systems, decision and control,x2198-4190 ;vvolume 507  aThis book proposes a solution to the problem of incorrect use of automation tools to perform complex design work. Currently, a large number of start-up projects are non-professional design bureaus that show a huge amount of their achievements. In reality, most of these achievements burst like soap bubbles. This is due to the low-quality and inefficient use of information technology in this industry. The book highlights advanced information technologies in the fields of design, machine learning, and computer vision0 aInformation Technology for Determining the Flight Performance of a Paraglider Wing -- Designing a Basic Model of an Unmanned Aerial Vehicle for the Subsequent Development of a Family of Samples with Different Purposes -- Transport Category Aircraft Fuselage Integrated Design -- Blind Evaluation of Noise Characteristics in Multichannel Images -- Directions of Using Branched Trajectories of Deter-mined Complex Dynamic Systems -- Using Krotov's Functions for the Prompt Synthesis Trajectory of Intelligent Info-communication Robot0 aOnline resource; title from PDF title page (SpringerLink, viewed November 15, 2023) 0aAerospace engineeringxInformation technology. 0aAerospace engineeringxAutomation. 6aAérospatiale (Ingénierie)xTechnologie de l'information. 6aAérospatiale (Ingénierie)xAutomatisation.1 aNechyporuk, Mykola,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20230462771 aPavlikov, Volodymyr,eeditor.1 aKrytskyi, Dmytro,eeditor.08iPrint version:z3031435788z9783031435782w(OCoLC)1392341057 0aStudies in systems, decision and control ;vv. 507.0http://id.loc.gov/a